# Phase 6: install / run / uninstall verification
# Performed from a CLEAN CLONE, not the working tree.

## 1. Fresh clone
$ git clone <repo> /tmp/ci-sim && cd /tmp/ci-sim

## 2. CI job 1 — no display server
$ cargo fmt --all --check                  -> OK
$ cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings -> OK
$ cargo test -- --test-threads=1           -> 63 + 14 + 59 + 1 = 137 passed, 0 failed
$ cargo build --release -p portscope-gtk -p portscope-cli -> OK

## 3. CI job 2 — translations
msgfmt --check-format --check-domain crates/gtk/po/zh_CN.po -> OK
untranslated entries: 0

## 4. CI job 3 — metadata
$ desktop-file-validate data/desktop/io.github.portscope.app.desktop -> OK
$ appstreamcli validate data/metainfo/io.github.portscope.app.metainfo.xml
  -> 1 warning: url-homepage-missing (documented open item, no repo yet)
$ test -f LICENSE && grep -q 'MIT License' LICENSE -> OK

## 5. Install into a temp prefix (no root)
$ PREFIX=/tmp/final-install ./scripts/install.sh
  Installed 15 files: 2 binaries, desktop entry, metainfo, 7 icon sizes +
  scalable, zh_CN catalogue, caches.

## 6. Launch the INSTALLED binary
$ HOME=/tmp/final-home  (settings.ini: language=zh_CN)
$ /tmp/final-install/bin/portscope
  -> runs, real data: 140 ports / 203 processes / 361 services
  -> interface in Simplified Chinese, proving the catalogue was found in
     <prefix>/share/locale rather than the development tree.
  Screenshot: evidence/screenshots/phase6-installed-run-zh.png

## 7. Uninstall
$ PREFIX=/tmp/final-install ./scripts/uninstall.sh
  -> no files remain under the prefix
  -> settings kept (documented behaviour; --purge removes them)

## Defects found by this verification (all fixed)
1. CRLF line endings: core.autocrlf=true converted the .desktop file on
   checkout, and desktop-file-validate rejected it. Added .gitattributes.
2. Illegal XML comment ('--strict' contains a double hyphen) made the metainfo
   unparseable. Fixed.
3. gettext does not resolve '..' in a bindtextdomain directory, so an installed
   PortScope started in English despite language=zh_CN. Path is now
   canonicalised.
4. uninstall.sh left two generated cache files behind. Fixed.
